# scan_secrets.py allow-list: <rule> <path glob>. Use sparingly, only for content that may not change.
# The trolley model (binary glTF): its compressed JPEG textures hold short random byte runs that read like a drive letter and a
# slash. Checked: its JSON chunk has no path, name or address, and its 12 JPEGs carry no metadata segments.
drive-path games/trolley/assets/trolley.glb
# The car battery prop (binary glTF, NVIDIA SimReady): float32 vertex data at one offset reads like a drive letter and a slash.
# Checked: its JSON chunk holds no path, name or address; its JPEGs carry no metadata segments.
drive-path games/trolley/assets/props/battery.glb
# The pallet prop (binary glTF, NVIDIA SimReady): float32 vertex data at one offset reads like a drive letter and a slash; checked as above.
drive-path games/trolley/assets/props/pallet_wood.glb
# The world's pallet rack (binary glTF, NVIDIA SimReady): a JPEG's compressed bytes at one offset read like a drive letter and a slash.
# Checked: its JSON chunk holds no path, name or address; its JPEGs carry no metadata segments.
drive-path games/trolley/assets/world/dock_pallet_rack.glb
# The world's utility cabinet (binary glTF, NVIDIA SimReady): float32 vertex data at one offset and a JPEG's compressed bytes at another
# read like a drive letter and a slash; checked as above.
drive-path games/trolley/assets/world/metro_utility_cabinet.glb
